  "observations": [
    "DamageUtil server-only mixed helper first vetoes BOTH if either damage source entity allied with target. It sets attachment lastDamage sentinel-1, remembers lastHurt, calls first hurt, regards first registered if returnedtrue OR sentinel changed (including0). It adds nominal amount1 to damageSoFar when observed lastDamage!=0; unchanged sentinel-1 also passes. It subtracts nominal first amount from current lastHurt with floor0, resets sentinel then calls second hurt. Nominal amount2 likewise accumulates if sentinel!=0. Finally writes max(original lastHurt,damageSoFar). No finally restoring field on throw.",
    "Actual onLivingHurtPost writes event.getNewDamage to LivingData AFTER other fire-unfreeze/player callbacks. The shared attachment is a scalar, no per-cast/source/reentry token, and not serialized in LivingData NBT. Post reaching0 and no Post reaching-1 are distinct to helper, but current code treats unchanged-1 as nominal contribution. This is source observation, not proof exact native hurt event dispatch or actual HP.",
    "If second hurt returnedtrue and first registered, helper explicitly broadcasts second source hurt entity byte and applies source-relative knockback; Player also gets selected generic/fire/drowning hurt sound. This is repaired secondary-hit presentation, not control-refusal reason. Returned Pair retains raw first/second hurt booleans, which differs from inferred first registration used for replay.",
    "SuperNova actual registered effect tick invokes this helper for living eligible caster.canAttack targets; only Pair.right fire bool gates extra radial knockback plus ignite5s. First accepted alone cannot trigger these extras. Effect scans each tick; no local hit-set. Nonliving branch calls ordinary projectile hurt. Tick1 effect sound/camera/particle requests are independent of individual target result.",
    "EntityMagicEffect resolves caster by saved UUID in current ServerLevel and caches until removed, requests link packet on successful resolution; helper nearbyCube uses entity AABB and excludes this effect only. Native actual spawn/link/LOS not certified. Supernova client/server tick discard checks do not return immediately, so no claim discarded entity stops remaining body on that invocation.",
    "Player SupernovaAbility actual active-section callback server creates registered SuperNova, addFreshEntity return ignored, then removes/reduces current SunsBlessing duration cost. It does not prove input admission/start/tick ordering. Earlier phase direct velocity pull and status/particles are contextual support0, not another candidate.",
    "MMCommon constructor registers EntityHandler REG, data attachments and ServerEventHandler on NeoForge bus. AbilityHandler installs Supernova in player types, only server sends activation if instance.canUse and invokes AbilityData.activateAbility then sends ID/index presentation. Actual AbilityData lifecycle and parent section progression still unread."
  ],
